---
title: Assumptions are not a brief
date: 2026-09-15
summary: A redesign request often starts with a solution. Here's how I turn it back into a problem we can actually measure.
tag: Process
color: blue
---

Most projects arrive with a solution already attached: "we need a new website", "the app needs a refresh". Sometimes that's right. Often it's an assumption nobody has checked.

## Turn the request into questions

Before any design work, I write down what we believe and what would prove it. "People don't know who we are" becomes "how many visitors reach the about page, and what do they do next?"

## Set a baseline

If there's no data yet, the first deliverable is a way to measure. It's not glamorous, but it's the only way to know later whether the work paid off.

## Then design

With a clear problem and a baseline, design decisions get easier to make and much easier to defend.
